direction: down
title: Spring Security 6 Servlet Filter Pipeline Architecture

Tomcat: Tomcat Servlet Container {
  style.fill: "#0B132B"
  style.stroke: "#0284C7"
  proxy: DelegatingFilterProxy
}

SpringBean: Spring ApplicationContext {
  style.fill: "#06201B"
  style.stroke: "#10B981"
  fcp: FilterChainProxy (springSecurityFilterChain)
}

Chain: SecurityFilterChain Pipeline {
  style.fill: "#0F172A"
  style.stroke: "#8B5CF6"
  cors: "1. CorsFilter"
  csrf: "2. CsrfFilter"
  jwt: "3. BearerTokenAuthenticationFilter"
  ex: "4. ExceptionTranslationFilter"
  authz: "5. AuthorizationFilter"
  cors -> csrf -> jwt -> ex -> authz
}

MVC: Spring MVC Core {
  style.fill: "#1E1B4B"
  style.stroke: "#8B5CF6"
  servlet: DispatcherServlet
  controller: "@RestController Handler Method"
  servlet -> controller
}

Tomcat.proxy -> SpringBean.fcp: Delegates to Spring Bean { style.stroke: "#38BDF8" }
SpringBean.fcp -> Chain.cors: Dispatches filter pipeline { style.stroke: "#10B981" }
Chain.authz -> MVC.servlet: Request passed (Principal verified) { style.stroke: "#34D399" }
